+# Password Hashing
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to hash passwords with argon2id. The stated rationale is that argon2id is a memory-hard algorithm and is much harder to crack than the previous choice, particularly against brute-force and dictionary attacks. No parameter values (memory cost, iterations, parallelism) have been recorded, so none are specified here.
